{% set local_problem %}
<p>On flat land, you can often get away with simple downspout extensions that deposit water a few feet from your foundation. On Arab's hillside lots, that approach doesn't work. Water deposited at your foundation flows downhill — but "downhill" often means along your foundation wall, concentrating at the lowest point of your home.</p>

<p>We've seen Arab homes where years of improper drainage have caused serious damage: cracked foundations, flooded basements and crawl spaces, collapsed retaining walls, and massive erosion. The repair costs can easily reach $10,000-30,000 or more.</p>

<p>Underground drainage solves these problems by capturing water at your downspouts and routing it through buried pipes to a safe discharge point well away from your home. The water is contained the entire distance, so it can't erode soil or collect where it shouldn't.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Underground drainage systems consist of buried pipes that connect your downspouts to a discharge point downhill from your home. Here's how we design and install them:</p>

<p><strong>Site Assessment:</strong> We evaluate your lot's slope, identify natural drainage patterns, locate the best discharge point, and plan the pipe route to avoid utilities and obstacles.</p>

<p><strong>Intake Connection:</strong> We connect to your downspouts with adapters that transition from the rectangular downspout to round drainage pipe. Some systems include catch basins for additional water collection.</p>

<p><strong>Pipe Installation:</strong> We trench to the appropriate depth, maintaining proper slope throughout. Pipes are bedded in gravel where needed for stability and drainage.</p>

<p><strong>Discharge Setup:</strong> The system terminates at a pop-up emitter, drainage ditch, or other suitable discharge point. We ensure water exits well away from any structures.</p>

<p><strong>Restoration:</strong> Trenches are backfilled and turf is replaced. Within a few weeks, you won't see evidence of the installation.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've installed underground drainage on many Arab hillside properties and understand the terrain's challenges. Rocky soil, tree roots, and varying slopes require experience and the right equipment — we have both.</p>

<p>Underground drainage is one of the most effective investments you can make to protect a hillside home. We design systems that work with your lot's natural grade, handle heavy mountain storms, and provide decades of protection. Based just 30 minutes away in Huntsville, we're your local experts in drainage solutions.</p>
{% endset %}
